BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[PA] Habitat Restoration at Eden Landing (Hayward)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T120000
DTSTAMP:20260923T174415Z
UID:savethebay-1355690@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Come join us at Eden Landing Ecological Reserve to help restor
 e former industrial salt ponds into healthy salt marsh habitat! This visio
 n includes turning vulnerable fields of invasive mustard and thistle into 
 resilient shoreline full of natives like California Poppy\, Sticky Monkeyf
 lower and Marsh Gumplant. We will be pulling the invasive species crowding
  our recently planted native species\, and will potentially be spreading m
 ulch around our native plants as well. We hope you will enjoy giving our b
 aby native plants the support they need to transform the land!\n\nAccessib
 ility: This program involves walking on a gravel trail and working on a sl
 oped dirt surface. There is a porta-potty onsite.\n\nPlease dress accordin
 g to the weather\, bring a water bottle and a snack. Gloves\, hand picks\,
  foam…\n\nSave The Bay recommends ages 8+\; under-16 must be accompanied
  by a parent/guardian and sign a waiver. 6-year-old eligibility varies per
  event — confirm with STB before registering.\n\nAges: 8+ recommended (6
 + with parent\, per-event confirmation)\nRegistration: required\nSource: h
 ttps://savesfbay.org/event/habitat-restoration-at-eden-landing-hayward-1jx
 wyay/\nLast synced: 2026-09-23 10:44 PDT
LOCATION:San Francisco Bay Area
URL:https://savesfbay.org/event/habitat-restoration-at-eden-landing-haywar
 d-1jxwyay/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[SM] ReScape Maintenance Qualification Training (MQT) - (Online)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T153000
DTSTAMP:20260923T174415Z
UID:flowstobay-19441-1790240400-1790263800@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Cost:  \n\n$695 Early Bird Price – last day August 22nd
 \n$695 Group Rate (please email info@rescapeca.org)\n$745 Regular Price
  – starting August 23rd\n\nDates: September 22\, 24\, 29 & October 1
 \, 2026 \nTime: 9 AM – 3:30 PM (Pacific Time)\n \nFormat: live online 
 via Zoom  \nGrounded in ReScape’s 8 Regenerative Principles\, this tr
 aining provides landscape maintenance professionals with cutting-edge tool
 s and expertise to create healthy\, climate-resilient landscapes while pro
 tecting local watersheds. Taught by leading experts\, the MQT offers hands
 -on learning in soil health\, irrigation\, plant care\, integrated pest ma
 nagement\, and more. \nThe MQT is open to everyone interested in expanding
  their knowledge of regenerative practices. It equips participants with ac
 tionable strategies to address climate change\, improve professional skill
 s\, and enhance business prospects. Participants gain: \n\nCost-Reduction
  Techniques: Strategies to minimize maintenance expenses\, chemical inputs
 \, water\, and energy consumption. Information on ROI\nExpert Training: In
 sights from industry leaders on Integrated Pest Management\, firescaping\,
  irrigation efficiency\, soil health\, and water conservation.\nRegenerati
 ve Practices for Increased ROI: Best practices for using recycled and salv
 aged materials\, carbon sequestration\, selecting plants suited to local c
 onditions\, and sourcing sustainable\, local products.\nHands-On Knowledge
 : Practical skills like sheet mulching\, soil sampling\, managing leaf deb
 ris/green waste\, and irrigation system maintenance.\nChecklist and planti
 ngs tools: a deep understanding of the watershed whole-systems approach to
  regenerative management.\nCompetitive Edge: Status as a ReScape Qualified
  Professional (RQP)\, offering credibility and expertise in regenerative l
 andscape practices.\nProfessional Benefits: A complimentary one-year ReSca
 pe Qualified Professional membership with an option to be listed in the Pr
 ofessional Directory for increased business visibility.\n\n Download the
  Maintenance Training Overview.  \n\n\n\nThese are the last courses on ou
 r 2026 calendar — secure your spot now by registering early. We encourag
 e you to share this with colleagues who would benefit! \nWe also offer cus
 tom private trainings if you’d prefer something tailored to your team’
 s schedule and focus areas — just reach out and we can explore what that
  could look like together. \nQuestions? Reply to this email or reach me at
  ryne@rescapeca.org. \nHere’s to building regenerative landscapes toget
 her\, \nRyne \nP.S. – Scholarship opportunities available: Staff and con
 tractors of StopWaste Member Agencies (Alameda County cities and agencie
 s) qualify for free training through partnership scholarships. Contact me 
 to learn more\, or to explore other available scholarship options. \nRyne 
 De Ocampo\, Training & Community Supervisor \nryne@rescapeca.org | resca
 peca.org \n  \nREGISTER HERE\n\nAges: Varies per event — many family-fr
 iendly. Confirm with event host.\nSource: https://flowstobay.org/calendar/
 rescape-maintenance-qualification-training-mqt-online-2/\nLast synced: 202
 6-09-23 10:44 PDT
LOCATION:Online\, CA\, United States
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/rescape-maintenance-qualification-trai
 ning-mqt-online-2/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[SM] Friends of Edgewood Natural Preserve: Weed Warriors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T120000
DTSTAMP:20260923T174415Z
UID:flowstobay-17539-1790326800-1790337600@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Come help the California Native Plant Society’s Edgewood Wee
 d Warriors program and protect Edgewood’s amazing biodiversity by contro
 lling and removing invasive\, non-native plants. We’ll have great opport
 unities to see native wildflowers and other plants\, and to learn about lo
 cal ecology from other volunteers and local experts.Teens are welcome\, bu
 t must each be accompanied by one of their own parents\; unaccompanied adu
 lt students must have proof of age. Friday sessions run year round… meet
 ing locations are determined weekly\, so contact us for more information (
 or join our email contact list). For more info and contact details go to h
 ttps://friendsofedgewood.org/habitat-restoration. \nEWW operates by permit
  from County Parks… please don’t do any weeding on your own! \nLocatio
 n: Edgewood County Park & Natural Preserve in San Mateo County. \nSIGN UP 
 HERE\n\nAges: Varies per event — many family-friendly. Confirm with even
 t host.\nSource: https://flowstobay.org/calendar/friends-of-edgewood-natur
 al-preserve-weed-warriors-2026-09-25/\nLast synced: 2026-09-23 10:44 PDT
LOCATION:Edgewood County Park & Natural Preserve\, CA\, United States
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/friends-of-edgewood-natural-preserve-w
 eed-warriors-2026-09-25/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[SM] Mussel Rock Beach Cleanup
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T110000
DTSTAMP:20260923T174415Z
UID:flowstobay-17534-1790413200-1790420400@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:About the Cleanup:\nTime: Fourth Saturday of the month from 9
 am-11am\, rain or shine. Check our online monthly calendar for exact dat
 es.\nWhere to Meet:  At the Mussel Rock carpark located at the lower coas
 tal end of Westline Drive by the second entrance to Allied Waste Transfer 
 Station.  Drive north past the junction of Skyline Drive\, avoiding the o
 ther Westline Drive that goes up a steep hill.\nParking:  Free parking is
  available all the time on any of the roads or at the car park at the meet
  up spot. Follow the signs to the car park so that you do not get lost on 
 the other Westline Drive that ends up above the Transfer Station.\nCleanup
  Areas: The team cleans up the streets\, bluffs\, car park and park\, itse
 lf\, as well as the beach if the tide is out far enough for our safety.  
 There is the Secret Waterfall nearby that is a good place to clean if you 
 are looking for excitement rappelling down a rope to the bluff and walking
  down to the beach.\nSupplies: Volunteers are encouraged to bring their ow
 n buckets and reusable gloves. Extra gloves\, buckets\, pickup sticks and 
 specific tools for this site cleanup will be provided while supplies last.
  The weather is unpredictable (very cold and windy\, although it can be su
 nny and warm).  Make sure to bring extra layers\, a hat\, sunblock\, wate
 r and snacks.\nLitter: The team usually picks up plastic bags\, bottles\,
  cigarettes and other household waste because this is where the Bay Area
 ’s trash is brought before it is transferred to other sites. Mussel Roc
 k Beach is a designated Japanese Tsunami Marine Debris Cleanup Program s
 ite\, and is the only one that has reported items to NOAA and GGNRA which 
 appear to have originated from Japan.\nRestrooms: Regrettably\, there are 
 no public restrooms at this site. \nSign Up Here!\n\nAges: Varies per even
 t — many family-friendly. Confirm with event host.\nSource: https://flow
 stobay.org/calendar/mussel-rock-beach-cleanup-4-2026-09-26/\nLast synced: 
 2026-09-23 10:44 PDT
LOCATION:Mussel Rock Beach – Meet at the Mussel Rock carpark located at 
 the lower coastal end of Westline Drive by the second entrance to Allied W
 aste Transfer Station.\, CA\, United States
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/mussel-rock-beach-cleanup-4-2026-09-26
 /
END:VEVENT
