BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[SM] California Sustainable Pest Management: Advanced Integrated P
 est Management (IPM) in the Urban Landscape  Advanced Professional Worksho
 p + Certification (Online)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261006T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261006T153000
DTSTAMP:20260923T174415Z
UID:flowstobay-19434-1791277200-1791300600@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Date: Tuesday\, October 6\, 2026Time: 9:00am – 3:30pm \nCo
 st:  \n\n$295 – Regular Admission – Advanced Professional Workshop\n
 \n\nReScape Certification (Available to RQPs only)*\n\n$295 – Certifica
 tion without Renewal\n$360 – Certification with 2 Year Qualification Ren
 ewal\n$395 – Certification with 2 Year Qualification Renewal and Directo
 ry Listing\n\n\n\nJoin us for our ReScape interactive Certification Worksh
 op. In January 2023\, California DPR Sustainable pest management (SPM) pu
 blished the “Accelerating Sustainable Pest Management Road Map for Cali
 fornia\,” an IPM approach that integrates various techniques and produc
 ts to promote healthy\, resilient ecosystems across diverse settings. It 
 talks about reduction of pest management risks and offers effective 
 solutions.   \nThis Workshop is a 6-hour deep dive into areas of foc
 us\, role\, programs\, and available resources in Sustainable Pest Managem
 ent (SPM) as governed by the Department of Pesticide Regulation (DPR) in C
 alifornia. The Workshop will provide you with a comprehensive understandi
 ng of pest management practices. ReScape’s 8 Principles for Regenerati
 ve Landscapes will reinforce a whole-systems approach.  Approved by DPR
  as a Continuing Education (CE) course\, individuals looking to renew thei
 r DPR license or certification will receive 5.5 CE hours. \nThis course wi
 ll equip you with the knowledge and skills necessary to implement sustaina
 ble and effective Integrated Pest Management (IPM) strategies. You will d
 elve into various aspects of pest management\, from understanding the foun
 dational principles of SPM to gaining proficiency in pest identification
 \, control and safety techniques. You will share issues and emerging tre
 nds you are seeing out in the field. We will explore the crucial role of I
 PM in creating healthy\, resilient ecosystems in diverse settings.  \nBy 
 the end of this course\, you will know regulations and guidelines gover
 ning pest management. Real-world case studies and industry best practices 
 will provide tools to implement IPM strategies effectively.   \n*Sele
 cting an option for a Certification with or without renewal is for ReScape
  Qualified Professionals (RQPs) only. RQPs are those who have completed on
 e or more of our multi-day Qualification Trainings. Please reach out to 
 ryne@rescapeca.org if you are not sure of your RQP status.\nIf you are no
 t an RQP\, you can still attend this Workshop. Simply selection the “Adv
 anced Professional Workshop” option. \nAs a reminder\, if you signed up 
 to receive a ReScape Certification for this Workshop\, please note that yo
 u will take a Certification Exam following the conclusion. Please reserve 
 an additional 15-30 minutes to complete the Exam.  \n\n\n\nThese are the 
 last courses on our 2026 calendar — secure your spot now by registering 
 early. We encourage you to share this with colleagues who would benefit! 
 \nWe also offer custom private trainings if you’d prefer something tailo
 red to your team’s schedule and focus areas — just reach out and we ca
 n explore what that could look like together. \nQuestions? Reply to this e
 mail or reach me at ryne@rescapeca.org. \nHere’s to building regenerati
 ve landscapes together\, \nRyne \nP.S. – Scholarship opportunities avail
 able: Staff and contractors of StopWaste Member Agencies (Alameda County
  cities and agencies) qualify for free training through partnership schola
 rships. Contact me to learn more\, or to explore other available scholarsh
 ip options. \nRyne De Ocampo\, Training & Community Supervisor \nryne@resc
 apeca.org | rescapeca.orgrescapeca.org \n  \nREGISTER HERE\n\nAges: Var
 ies per event — many family-friendly. Confirm with event host.\nSource: 
 https://flowstobay.org/calendar/california-sustainable-pest-management-adv
 anced-integrated-pest-management-ipm-in-the-urban-landscape-advanced-profe
 ssional-workshop-certification-online/\nLast synced: 2026-09-23 10:44 PDT
LOCATION:Online\, CA\, United States
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/california-sustainable-pest-management
 -advanced-integrated-pest-management-ipm-in-the-urban-landscape-advanced-p
 rofessional-workshop-certification-online/
END:VEVENT
