BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[SM] Mussel Rock Beach Cleanup
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T110000
DTSTAMP:20260923T174415Z
UID:flowstobay-17751-1792832400-1792839600@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:About the Cleanup:\nTime: Fourth Saturday of the month from 9
 am-11am\, rain or shine. Check our online monthly calendar for exact dat
 es.\nWhere to Meet:  At the Mussel Rock carpark located at the lower coas
 tal end of Westline Drive by the second entrance to Allied Waste Transfer 
 Station.  Drive north past the junction of Skyline Drive\, avoiding the o
 ther Westline Drive that goes up a steep hill.\nParking:  Free parking is
  available all the time on any of the roads or at the car park at the meet
  up spot. Follow the signs to the car park so that you do not get lost on 
 the other Westline Drive that ends up above the Transfer Station.\nCleanup
  Areas: The team cleans up the streets\, bluffs\, car park and park\, itse
 lf\, as well as the beach if the tide is out far enough for our safety.  
 There is the Secret Waterfall nearby that is a good place to clean if you 
 are looking for excitement rappelling down a rope to the bluff and walking
  down to the beach.\nSupplies: Volunteers are encouraged to bring their ow
 n buckets and reusable gloves. Extra gloves\, buckets\, pickup sticks and 
 specific tools for this site cleanup will be provided while supplies last.
  The weather is unpredictable (very cold and windy\, although it can be su
 nny and warm).  Make sure to bring extra layers\, a hat\, sunblock\, wate
 r and snacks.\nLitter: The team usually picks up plastic bags\, bottles\,
  cigarettes and other household waste because this is where the Bay Area
 ’s trash is brought before it is transferred to other sites. Mussel Roc
 k Beach is a designated Japanese Tsunami Marine Debris Cleanup Program s
 ite\, and is the only one that has reported items to NOAA and GGNRA which 
 appear to have originated from Japan.\nRestrooms: Regrettably\, there are 
 no public restrooms at this site. \nSign Up Here!\n\nAges: Varies per even
 t — many family-friendly. Confirm with event host.\nSource: https://flow
 stobay.org/calendar/mussel-rock-beach-cleanup-4-2026-10-24/\nLast synced: 
 2026-09-23 10:44 PDT
LOCATION:Mussel Rock Beach – Meet at the Mussel Rock carpark located at 
 the lower coastal end of Westline Drive by the second entrance to Allied W
 aste Transfer Station.\, CA\, United States
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/mussel-rock-beach-cleanup-4-2026-10-24
 /
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[SM] San Mateo Countywide Half-Price Rain Barrel Sale: City of Hal
 f Moon Bay Event (Place Order ASAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T120000
DTSTAMP:20260923T174415Z
UID:flowstobay-19582-1792832400-1792843200@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:The annual Half-Price Rain Barrel Sale is back for its sixth y
 ear! San Mateo County residents and businesses can purchase up to two high
 -quality 50-gallon rain barrels for only $85 each (pre-tax\, regularly $15
 2)\, which is 44% below market price. Pick up your order at one of two con
 venient countywide events. \nPlus\, earn money back from the local rebate 
 program after installation to make your purchase low- or no-cost: \n\n$50 
 through the countywide rebate (for up to two barrels)\nAn additional $50 i
 f your water provider is one of 10 participating agencies\n\nDon’t wait!
  See below for rain barrel sales information: \n\nCity of San Mateo event 
 on October 17 (9am – 12pm): Sales open until October 4 at 11pm or while 
 supplies last\nCity of Half Moon Bay event on October 24 (9am – 12pm): S
 ales open until October 11 at 11pm or while supplies last\n\nSales can clo
 se sooner if we run out of stock—get yours before they’re gone! \nThe 
 address for the event will be included in your purchase order. \nLearn mor
 e\, check your rebate eligibility\, and place your order here. \nDon’t 
 miss your chance to join the rain barrel movement this year! \n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n*Orders must be picked up at the event location listed on your purchase 
 order.\n\nAges: Varies per event — many family-friendly. Confirm with ev
 ent host.\nSource: https://flowstobay.org/calendar/san-mateo-countywide-ha
 lf-price-rain-barrel-sale-city-of-half-moon-bay-event/\nLast synced: 2026-
 09-23 10:44 PDT
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/san-mateo-countywide-half-price-rain-b
 arrel-sale-city-of-half-moon-bay-event/
END:VEVENT
